━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Markup is facet of FunctionEmitter
    sees Assignments
    sees Calls
    sees LiveActions
    sees Styles

────────────────────
+ do emit-content
    - id SyntaxId
    - link ContentLink

` A line of a markup element's body that the element takes: its value is evaluated, takes
` the conversion recorded for it as an argument, and is given to the method the type pass
` found for it, called on the element whose body is being run. What the method answers is
` dropped, but where the line is an element a name is declared for: the name then holds the
` answer, converted as a value assigned to it. A line that is a markup branch region or a
` markup loop region is the region, whose action is made once the element has taken it. A line
` whose value read something tracked is evaluated while a live action of its own is open, whose
` trackers note what it reads, and the action is made once the element has taken the value, as
` that of an attribute is (`give-again`), and what the element took of it is kept for the action
` to replace (`keep-taken`). An element named for the property its class's markup declares for
` it, which no local is declared for, gives the property what the element took it as, or the
` object where that is nothing; one a local is declared for gives it what the local holds, which
` the environment of a function the element is written in may keep. A slot outlet that is a
` branch region is written at its parameter (`region-site`).
. site = tree.region-site(id)
. region = facts.branch-region-of(unit.reading, site)
. looped = facts.loop-region-of(unit.reading, id)
. live = tables.live-statement-of(unit.reading, id) if !region && !looped && !rerunning && unit.reading == unit.instance
. trackers = no-local
. made = Typed(make-operand(.operand-void, 0), no-type)
if region
    made = emit-branch(site, region)
else if looped
    made = emit-loop(id, looped)
else if live
    trackers = open-trackers(id)
    live-actions += LiveTrackers(trackers, trackers)
    made = emit-expression(id)
    live-actions.pop()
else
    made = emit-expression(id)
. converted = convert(id, .reason-argument, made)
. top = content-hosts.length
if top == 0 || content-hosts[top - 1].type != link.parent
    refuse(.refused-statement, id)
    =
if converted.type != link.taken
    refuse(.refused-conversion, id)
    =
. answer = call-protocol
    - id
    - link.call
    - content-hosts[top - 1].operand
    - link.parent
    - converted.operand
    - link.taken
    - false
if link.append != no-instance
    . mark = pending.length
    pending += content-hosts[top - 1].operand
    pending += answer.operand
    call-instance(link.append, id, mark)
. answered = answer.type
if live
    . whole = link.append != no-instance || answered != types.void-type
    keep-taken(id, (if whole then answer else made).operand, if whole then answered else made.type)
if live
    give-again(id, trackers, content-hosts[top - 1].operand, link.parent)
    =
if region
    own-branch(site, region, made.operand)
    =
if looped
    own-loop(id, looped, made.operand)
    =
if link.answers == no-type
    . named = facts.named-store-of(unit.reading, id)
    if named != U32.max
        match? tree.nodes[id]
            | .node-markup(row)
                if !declares-element(id, row.id)
                    . gives = answered != no-type && answered != types.void-type
                    store-named(id, named, if gives then answer else made)
                    =
                . slot = local-slot(row.id, id, true, false, true)
                . outer = is-captured(slot) && tables.slot-functions[slot] != unit.own-scope
                . held = if outer then find-captured(slot, id).type else facts.slot-type(unit.instance, slot-offset(slot, id))
                . kept = if outer then read-captured(slot, id, held) else slot-value(slot, id, held)
                store-named(id, named, Typed(kept.operand, held))
if link.answers == no-type
    =
if answered != link.answers
    refuse(.refused-conversion, id)
    =
. raw = answer
answer = convert(id, .reason-assignment, answer)
match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-markup(row)
        . slot = local-slot(row.id, id, true, false, true)
        if is-captured(slot) && tables.slot-functions[slot] != unit.own-scope
            keep-captured(slot, answer.operand, answer.type, id)
        else
            keep-state(slot, answer.operand, answer.type, id)
. named = facts.named-store-of(unit.reading, id)
if named != U32.max
    store-named(id, named, raw)

────────────────────
_ do emit-branch Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - region BranchRegion

` A markup branch region, as the reference makes one:
` the function of each arm, made the `MarkupBranchBuilder` recorded at the arm, in a
` list made at the `if`; the index of the arm whose condition holds, read while a live action
` of the region's own is open, whose trackers are kept to make the action with once the
` element has taken the region; and the region the markup runtime makes of them for the
` element being built. The batch in force is kept first for the arms, which the region builds
` as it is made, and the region is put under the batch found for the host. The arms of a match
` region read its subject again where the host is kept, which is first done here.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. top = content-hosts.length
if top == 0 || content-hosts[top - 1].type != region.host
    refuse(.refused-statement, id)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
if region.rooted
    keep-batch(id)
if tree.nodes[id] is .node-match-expression
    keep-captured(channel-slot(id), content-hosts[top - 1].operand, region.host, id)
. start = given.length
. count U32
for arm in tree.region-arms(id)
    . built = convert(arm, .reason-markup-arm, emit-closure(tree.region-arm-body(arm)))
    given += Typed(apart(built, arm, true), built.type)
    count += 1
. list = nothing
list = build-list(id, RowRange'SyntaxId(0, count), region.list, start, false).operand
drop-given(start)
. trackers = open-trackers(id)
live-actions += LiveTrackers(trackers, trackers)
. selected = emit-arm-index(id, region.selected)
live-actions.pop()
. mark = pending.length
pending += content-hosts[top - 1].operand
pending += list
pending += selected.operand
. made = raising-call(id, region.create, mark)
put-under-batch
    - id
    - region.ensure
    - region.hosted
    - made.operand
    - instances.signatures[region.create].returns
branch-trackers += trackers
= Typed(made.operand, instances.signatures[region.create].returns)

────────────────────
_ do own-branch
    - id SyntaxId
    - region BranchRegion
    - made Operand

` The action of a markup branch region, once the element has taken the region: the element and
` the region are kept in the locals no name reaches declared at the `if`, for the function that
` selects the arm again, and the action, made by the markup runtime with the trackers the
` conditions noted and a callback that runs that function with the environment in force here,
` given the element as the host, or the batch found for it where the type pass found one, is
` owned by the element and marked structural.
. trackers = branch-trackers[branch-trackers.length - 1]
branch-trackers.pop()
. slot = channel-slot(id)
. code = tables.instance-functions[region.updater]
. top = content-hosts.length
if slot == no-slot || code == no-function || top == 0
    refuse(.refused-statement, id)
    =
. host = content-hosts[top - 1].operand
keep-captured(slot, host, region.host, id)
keep-captured(slot + 1, made, instances.signatures[region.create].returns, id)
. callback = make-callback(tables.live-adapter-of(code), written-environment(id), id)
. owner = if region.rooted || region.hosted then region-batch(id, region.hosted) else convert(id, .reason-markup-host, Typed(host, region.host)).operand
. mark = pending.length
pending += load-local(trackers, id)
pending += callback
pending += owner
. action = raising-call(id, region.action, mark)
attach-action(host, action.operand, id)
. marking = pending.length
pending += action.operand
pending += structural-owner(id, host, region.host, region.structural).operand
do raising-call(id, region.structural, marking)

────────────────────
_ do emit-loop Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - region LoopRegion

` A markup loop region, as the reference makes one:
` the container, read while a live action of the region's own is open, whose trackers are kept
` to make the action with once the element has taken the region, and converted to the source the
` type pass recorded at the container where it is no collection; the function that builds each
` row, made the builder recorded at the `for`, and that keys it, where the loop is keyed, made
` the `MarkupKeyBuilder` recorded at its clause; and the region the markup runtime makes of
` them for the element being built. The batch in force is kept first for the rows, which the
` region builds as it is made, and the region is put under the batch found for the host.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. top = content-hosts.length
. container = tree.region-container(id)
if top == 0 || content-hosts[top - 1].type != region.host || container == 0
    refuse(.refused-statement, id)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
if region.rooted
    keep-batch(id)
. trackers = open-trackers(id)
live-actions += LiveTrackers(trackers, trackers)
. source = emit-expression(container)
live-actions.pop()
if source.type != region.source
    source = convert(container, .reason-argument, source)
if source.type != region.source
    refuse(.refused-conversion, container)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-for-block(row)
        . built = convert(id, .reason-markup-row, emit-closure(row.body))
        if region.adapts != no-instance
            . filter = tree.when-clause(row.loop)
            . tester = if filter != 0 then convert(filter, .reason-markup-key, emit-closure(filter)).operand else nothing
            . adapting = pending.length
            pending += content-hosts[top - 1].operand
            pending += built.operand
            if filter != 0
                pending += tester
            built = raising-call(id, region.adapts, adapting)
        . keyed = tree.keyed-clause(row.loop)
        . keyer = if keyed != 0 then convert(keyed, .reason-markup-key, emit-closure(keyed)).operand else nothing
        . mark = pending.length
        pending += content-hosts[top - 1].operand
        pending += built.operand
        if keyed != 0
            pending += keyer
        pending += source.operand
        . made = raising-call(id, region.create, mark)
        put-under-batch
            - id
            - region.ensure
            - region.hosted
            - made.operand
            - instances.signatures[region.create].returns
        branch-trackers += trackers
        = Typed(made.operand, instances.signatures[region.create].returns)
refuse(.refused-statement, id)
= Typed(nothing, no-type)

────────────────────
+ do emit-selector
    - declared SyntaxId
    - id SyntaxId

. live = instances.live
if live.previous == no-instance || live.next == no-instance
    refuse(.refused-function, declared)
    =
. previous = ir.add-local(managed-layout)
store-local(previous, call-instance(live.previous, id, pending.length).operand, id)
. next = ir.add-local(managed-layout)
store-local(next, call-instance(live.next, id, pending.length).operand, id)
live-actions += LiveTrackers(previous, next)
. selected = emit-arm-index(id, returns-type)
live-actions.pop()
return-value(selected.operand, declared)

────────────────────
+ do emit-row-region ?! Refused
    - declared SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId

. parent = make-operand(.operand-argument, 2)
. type = instances.argument-type(unit.instance, 1)
. batch = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. root = facts.region-root-of(unit.reading, body)
if root
    batch = read-captured(root.slot, body, root.batch).operand
    if root.ensure != no-instance
        . host = convert(body, .reason-markup-host, Typed(parent, type))
        . given = convert-from(body, .reason-markup-root, batch)
        . mark = pending.length
        pending += host.operand
        pending += given.operand
        call-instance(root.ensure, body, mark)
content-hosts += Typed(parent, type)
content-roots += batch
emit-block(body)
content-hosts.pop()
content-roots.pop()
emit-end(declared)

────────────────────
_ do own-loop
    - id SyntaxId
    - region LoopRegion
    - made Operand

` The action of a markup loop region, once the element has taken the region: the element and the
` region are kept in the locals no name reaches declared at the `for`, for the function that reads
` the container again, and the action, made by the markup runtime with the trackers the container
` noted and a callback that runs that function with the environment in force here, given the region
` as the host, or the batch in force where there is one, is owned by the region and marked
` structural.
. trackers = branch-trackers[branch-trackers.length - 1]
branch-trackers.pop()
. slot = channel-slot(id)
. code = tables.instance-functions[region.updater]
. top = content-hosts.length
if slot == no-slot || code == no-function || top == 0
    refuse(.refused-statement, id)
    =
. made-type = instances.signatures[region.create].returns
keep-captured(slot, content-hosts[top - 1].operand, region.host, id)
keep-captured(slot + 1, made, made-type, id)
. callback = make-callback(tables.live-adapter-of(code), written-environment(id), id)
. owner = if region.rooted then region-batch(id, false) else convert(id, .reason-markup-host, Typed(made, made-type)).operand
. mark = pending.length
pending += load-local(trackers, id)
pending += callback
pending += owner
. action = raising-call(id, region.action, mark)
attach-action(made, action.operand, id)
. marking = pending.length
pending += action.operand
pending += structural-owner(id, made, made-type, region.structural).operand
do raising-call(id, region.structural, marking)

────────────────────
_ do structural-owner Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - owner Operand
    - type TypeId
    - call InstanceId

` The host that owns the action of a markup region, as the optional the call that marks the
` action structural takes: the parent of a branch or the region of a loop, converted where the
` type pass recorded it as a markup host, and nothing where it is none.
. fact = facts.first-conversion(unit.reading, id)
while fact != no-fact
    if facts.conversions[fact].reason == .reason-markup-structural
        . host = convert(id, .reason-markup-host, Typed(owner, type))
        = convert(id, .reason-markup-structural, host)
    fact = facts.conversions[fact].next
. optional = types.child-type(instances.signatures[call].args, 1)
= empty-optional(optional, layout-of(optional, id))

────────────────────
_ do keep-batch
    - id SyntaxId

` Keeps the batch in force where a markup region is written in the third local no name
` reaches declared at the `if` or `for`, which the functions that build its arms or rows read.
. slot = channel-slot(id)
. batch = if content-roots.length != 0 then outer-root else make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
    .. outer-root = content-roots[content-roots.length - 1]
if slot == no-slot || operand-kind(batch) == .operand-void
    refuse(.refused-statement, id)
    =
. field = find-captured(slot + 2, id)
keep-captured(slot + 2, batch, field.type, id)

────────────────────
_ do region-batch Operand
    - id SyntaxId
    - hosted Bool

` The batch the reference finds for the host of a markup region: the host itself where it is
` one, converted at the `if` or `for`, else the one in force.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. top = content-hosts.length
if hosted && top != 0
    = convert(id, .reason-markup-batch, content-hosts[top - 1]).operand
if hosted || content-roots.length == 0 || void-root
    refuse(.refused-statement, id)
    = nothing
.. void-root = operand-kind(content-roots[content-roots.length - 1]) == .operand-void
= content-roots[content-roots.length - 1]

────────────────────
_ do put-under-batch
    - id SyntaxId
    - ensure InstanceId
    - hosted Bool
    - made Operand
    - type TypeId

` Puts the region a markup region made under the batch found for its host, where the type pass
` found one, as the markup runtime's `ensure-markup-root` does, given the region as a host and
` the batch as the optional it takes.
if ensure == no-instance
    =
. batch = region-batch(id, hosted)
. region = convert(id, .reason-markup-region, Typed(made, type))
. given = convert-from(id, .reason-markup-root, batch)
. mark = pending.length
pending += region.operand
pending += given.operand
call-instance(ensure, id, mark)

────────────────────
+ do emit-markup Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - name SyntaxId
    - type-id SyntaxId
    - args RowRange'SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId

` A markup element: its object, with the lines of its body run as its content, the object being the
` element they are given to. Where it is a statement, the objects of the elements it declares names
` for are made first (`raise-elements`). The object of an element a block declares a name for is read
` from the name: one this function has not made has no shape. One whose name is placed is made here
` and given to the name. A body a function of its own builds into the default slot's node is no
` content here.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. made = nothing
. type = no-type
raise-elements(id)
if facts.is-raised(unit.reading, id)
    . slot = local-slot(name, id, true, false, true)
    if built.find(id) == null
        refuse(.refused-expression, id)
        = Typed(nothing, no-type)
    type = facts.slot-type(unit.instance, slot-offset(slot, id))
    made = slot-value(slot, id, type).operand
else
    . element = make-element(id, type-id, args)
    made = element.operand
    type = element.type
    if names-placed(name)
        name-element(id, name, element)
. root = batch-root(id, type-id, Typed(made, type))
if body != 0 && !is-closure(facts.node-type(unit.reading, body))
    content-hosts += Typed(made, type)
    content-roots += root
    emit-block(body)
    content-hosts.pop()
    content-roots.pop()
mount-root(id, type-id, made, type, root)
= Typed(made, type)

────────────────────
_ declares-element Bool
    - element SyntaxId
    - name SyntaxId

` Whether a block declares a local for a markup element's name, in the function whose facts
` are being read.
|? binding == no-binding
    false
??
    resolution.kind == .resolve-slot && bindings.slots[resolution.slot].group == element

.. binding = instances.rows[unit.reading].binding
.. resolution = bindings.resolution-of(binding, name)

────────────────────
_ names-placed Bool
    - name SyntaxId

` Whether a markup element's name is placed: given the element's object where the element is
` written, as no block made it where it starts.
|? name == 0 || binding == no-binding
    false
??
    resolution.kind == .resolve-slot && (bindings.slots[resolution.slot].flags /and/ SlotFlag.slot-placed) != 0

.. binding = instances.rows[unit.reading].binding
.. resolution = bindings.resolution-of(binding, name)

────────────────────
_ do batch-root Operand
    - id SyntaxId
    - type-id SyntaxId
    - made Typed

` The batch of markup in force in the body of a markup element, a `MarkupRootElement`: the element
` itself where its class is a batch, else the one in force where the element is written, if
` any. An element of a markup host is put under it first, given as the `MarkupRootElement?` the
` markup runtime takes.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. inherited = if content-roots.length != 0 then content-roots[content-roots.length - 1] else nothing
. root = facts.element-root-of(unit.reading, id)
if !root
    = inherited
. batch = inherited
if root.owns
    batch = convert(type-id, .reason-markup-batch, made).operand
if root.ensure != no-instance
    if operand-kind(batch) == .operand-void
        refuse(.refused-expression, id)
        = nothing
    . host = convert(type-id, .reason-markup-host, made)
    . given = convert-from(type-id, .reason-markup-root, batch)
    . mark = pending.length
    pending += host.operand
    pending += given.operand
    call-instance(root.ensure, id, mark)
= batch

────────────────────
_ do mount-root
    - id SyntaxId
    - type-id SyntaxId
    - made Operand
    - type TypeId
    - batch Operand

` Mounts a markup element that is no line of another as a root of the batch in force, once
` its body has run.
. root = facts.element-root-of(unit.reading, id)
if !root || root.mount == no-instance
    =
if operand-kind(batch) == .operand-void
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    =
. host = convert(type-id, .reason-markup-host, Typed(made, type))
. given = convert-from(type-id, .reason-markup-root, batch)
. mark = pending.length
pending += host.operand
pending += given.operand
call-instance(root.mount, id, mark)

────────────────────
+ do raise-elements
    - block SyntaxId

` Makes the object of each named markup element the type pass kept for a block of markup content,
` where it starts, or for a statement, where it runs, in order, and declares the element's name as
` a local that holds it.
. raised = facts.first-raised(unit.reading, block)
while raised != U32.max
    . fact = facts.raised-elements[raised]
    raise-element(fact.element)
    raised = fact.next

────────────────────
+ do raise-element
    - element SyntaxId

` Makes the object of a named markup element and declares its name as a local that holds it.
match? tree.nodes[element]
    | .node-markup(row)
        . made = make-element(element, row.type-id, row.args)
        name-element(element, row.id, made)

────────────────────
_ do name-element
    - element SyntaxId
    - name SyntaxId
    - made Typed

` Gives the name of a markup element its cell and stores the element's object there, as a
` declaration of a local with that value does: one some read tracks tells no read of it. A
` name a function this one is written in declares is kept in its environment.
. slot = local-slot(name, element, true, false, true)
. offset = slot-offset(slot, element)
. type = if is-captured(slot) && tables.slot-functions[slot] != unit.own-scope then find-captured(slot, element).type else facts.slot-type(unit.instance, offset)
if type == no-type || type == invalid-type || type != made.type
    refuse(.refused-statement, element)
    =
. layout = layout-of(type, element)
built += element
if is-captured(slot)
    keep-captured(slot, made.operand, type, element)
    =
. local = ir.add-local(layout, (bindings.slots[slot].flags /and/ SlotFlag.slot-address-taken) != 0)
unit.cells[offset] = local
store-local(local, made.operand, element)

────────────────────
_ do make-element Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - type-id SyntaxId
    - args RowRange'SyntaxId

` The object of a markup element, as its constructor makes it for its arguments and its
` attributes.
` 1. The constructor is called as a call written with the arguments is: an attribute that
`    names a parameter fills it, and the value of each other attribute is given after the
`    arguments. Each argument is kept as it was evaluated, before the call converted it, and
`    each attribute as given: converted to the property's type, and then, where it fills a
`    parameter, to the parameter's, as the call converted it.
`    The values given to the style rules written on the element are evaluated after the
`    attributes, before the call (`emit-rule-values`).
` 2. The object is kept for the functions that read its members by name alone, the gates of
`    the style rules written on it among them (`keep-element`). The state cells of the `when`s
`    around the rules written in rules the element sees, made before the call (`make-cells`),
`    are bound (`bind-cells`). The style rules the element applies run, then each attribute
`    that declares a style property declares it, in the order written.
` 3. Each value the type pass bound to a property is stored in the property: the
`    attributes, then the arguments, each in the order written. An argument takes the
`    conversion recorded for it as a value assigned. An attribute a setter answers is given
`    to the setter instead, in its place among them. Then the element's style site, if it has
`    one, is made ready.
` 4. Each attribute whose value read something tracked is given a live action, in the order
`    written, owned by the object, which gives it again: the object is kept where that
`    function reaches it. Then each argument given by position whose value did, so.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. own-styling = styling
. start = element-given.length
. filling = element-filled.length
. setting = setter-given.length
. valued = rule-givens.length
. lively = attribute-trackers.length
. arguing = argument-trackers.length
styling = styling.element = if facts.first-element-store(unit.reading, id) != U32.max || writes-attributes(id) then id else 0
styling = styling.valued = if gives-rule-values(id) then id else 0
make-cells(id)
. made = emit-call(id, type-id, args)
. type = made.type
styling = own-styling
keep-element(id, made.operand, type)
bind-cells(id, made.operand)
. association = declare-styles(id, made.operand, type)
while rule-givens.length > valued
    rule-givens.pop()
. store = facts.first-element-store(unit.reading, id)
while store != U32.max
    . fact = facts.element-stores[store]
    . place = start + fact.argument
    if fact.setter != 0
        set-attribute(fact.setter, made.operand, type, setting + fact.argument)
    else if place >= element-given.length
        refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    else
        . stored = element-given[place]
        if fact.converted != 0
            stored = convert(fact.converted, .reason-assignment, stored)
        store-argument(made.operand, type, fact.property, stored.operand, stored.type, id)
    store = fact.next
while element-given.length > start
    element-given.pop()
while element-filled.length > filling
    element-filled.pop()
while setter-given.length > setting
    setter-given.pop()
finish-styles(id, made.operand, type, association)
for position in lively .. < attribute-trackers.length
    give-again(attribute-trackers[position].member, attribute-trackers[position].trackers, made.operand, type)
for position in arguing .. < argument-trackers.length
    give-again(argument-trackers[position].member, argument-trackers[position].trackers, made.operand, type)
follow-bound(id, made.operand, type)
while attribute-trackers.length > lively
    attribute-trackers.pop()
while argument-trackers.length > arguing
    argument-trackers.pop()
= Typed(made.operand, type)

────────────────────
_ do follow-bound
    - id SyntaxId
    - made Operand
    - type TypeId

` Gives each binding of a markup element the action that stores back what the element holds as
` it changes: its first run only notes the read of the element's property, so that the place
` keeps the value it gave the element.
match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-markup(element)
        match? tree.nodes[element.body]
            | .node-block(block)
                for statement in tree.children[block.body]
                    match? tree.nodes[statement]
                        | .node-assign(attribute)
                            if attribute.op == .bind-op
                                . name = tree.identifier-name(attribute.lhs)
                                if !name
                                    refuse(.refused-statement, statement)
                                    =
                                . trackers = open-trackers(attribute.lhs)
                                live-actions += LiveTrackers(trackers, trackers)
                                track(attribute.lhs, made, name)
                                live-actions.pop()
                                give-again(statement, trackers, made, type, attribute.lhs)

────────────────────
_ do set-attribute
    - target SyntaxId
    - made Operand
    - type TypeId
    - place Size

` Gives the object of a markup element, once made, the value of an attribute a setter
` answers, kept where it was evaluated, by calling the setter the type pass chose at the
` attribute's name.
. call = own-call(target)
if call == no-fact || facts.calls[call].form != .call-setter || place >= setter-given.length
    refuse(.refused-expression, target)
    =
. callee = facts.calls[call].callee
if callee == no-instance || facts.calls[call].is-partial || !is-callable(callee) || other-arity
    refuse(.refused-expression, target)
    =
.. other-arity = instances.signatures[callee].args.count != 1
if setter-given[place].type != instances.argument-type(callee, 0)
    refuse(.refused-conversion, target)
    =
. receiver = convert(target, .reason-receiver, Typed(made, type))
if receiver.type != instances.rows[callee].self-type
    refuse(.refused-conversion, target)
. mark = pending.length
pending += receiver.operand
pending += setter-given[place].operand
call-method(callee, target, mark)

────────────────────
_ do hold-outlet-cells LocalId
    - id SyntaxId

` Holds, while the function that builds what a slot outlet mounts runs, the state cells the
` outlet holds (`OutletCell`), each by where it was made, after a mark of those held already,
` which it answers in a local of its own, as the reference's `withMarkupOutletStyleStateCells`
` holds them; none where it holds none.
. mark = no-local
for held in facts.outlet-cells
    if held.instance != unit.reading || held.outlet != id
        continue
    . local = cell-local(held.cell)
    if local == no-local
        refuse(.refused-expression, id)
        = no-local
    if mark == no-local
        . runtime = facts.style-runtime
        mark = ir.add-local(layout-of(instances.signatures[runtime.outlet-mark].returns, id))
        store-local(mark, call-instance(runtime.outlet-mark, id, pending.length).operand, id)
    . first = pending.length
    pending += integer(.machine-u32, tables.state-key-number(facts.scope-cells[held.cell].key))
    pending += load-local(local, id)
    do call-instance(facts.style-runtime.outlet-push, id, first)
= mark

────────────────────
_ do give-again
    - statement SyntaxId
    - trackers LocalId
    - made Operand
    - type TypeId
    - site SyntaxId = 0

` The live action of an attribute whose value read something tracked: the element's object
` is kept in the local no name reaches declared at the attribute, and the action, with the
` trackers the value noted and a callback that runs the attribute's function with the
` environment in force here, is owned by the object. That of an argument given by position
` keeps the object in the one declared at the element. The action of an element of a markup
` host is made by the markup runtime, given the element as its host, or where the type pass
` made it with a batch, given the element where it is the batch and else the one in force. That
` of a line of the element's body that gives content is made as an attribute's is, and that of a
` line of an arm's body is given what the arm's function is given, converted at the line. The
` action that stores back what a binding's element holds is made at the `site` it is written at.
. at = if site != 0 then site else statement
. row = tables.live-statement-of(unit.reading, at)
. element = tree.argument-element(statement)
. slot = if element != 0 then channel-slot(element) else line-keeper(statement)
. code = if row && row.rerun != no-instance then tables.instance-functions[row.rerun] else no-function
if code == no-function || slot == no-slot
    refuse(.refused-statement, at)
    =
if site == 0
    keep-captured(slot, made, type, statement)
if row!.owned == no-instance
    . action = make-action
        - load-local(trackers, at)
        - tables.live-adapter-of(code)
        - written-environment(at)
        - at
    attach-action(made, action.operand, at)
    =
. callback = make-callback(tables.live-adapter-of(code), written-environment(at), at)
. written = if element != 0 then element else tree.attribute-element(statement)
if written == 0
    written = tree.content-element(statement)
. type-id SyntaxId = if written == 0 then statement else 0u32
match? tree.nodes[written]
    | .node-markup(row)
        type-id = row.type-id
    | .node-slot-outlet(row)
        type-id = row.type-id
. owner = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
if row!.rooted
    . root = facts.element-root-of(unit.reading, written)
    if root && root.owns
        owner = convert(type-id, .reason-markup-batch, Typed(made, type)).operand
    else if content-roots.length != 0
        owner = content-roots[content-roots.length - 1]
    if operand-kind(owner) == .operand-void
        refuse(.refused-statement, statement)
else
    owner = convert(type-id, .reason-markup-host, Typed(made, type)).operand
. mark = pending.length
pending += load-local(trackers, at)
pending += callback
pending += owner
. action = raising-call(at, row!.owned, mark)
attach-action(made, action.operand, at)

────────────────────
+ do emit-attributes
    - id SyntaxId
    - callee InstanceId
    - fact CallFact
    - count U32

` Evaluates the attributes of a markup element that its constructor is given after its
` `count` arguments, in the order written: each takes the conversion recorded at its line as a
` value assigned, and is kept. One that names a parameter fills it; the place among the values
` kept of each other one is kept too, as the constructor is given those after its parameters.
` One whose value reads something tracked is evaluated in a live action of its own, whose
` trackers are kept to make the action with. One that declares a style is evaluated once the
` object is made, and one a setter answers is kept apart, for the setter (`set-attribute`). One
` the constructor is not given at the place it is written at has no shape here.
. given U32
. written U32
. declared = unfilled - instances.rows[callee].carried - instances.rows[callee].slots.count
    .. unfilled = instances.signatures[callee].args.count - instances.rows[callee].fills.count
match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-markup(element)
        match? tree.nodes[element.body]
            | .node-block(block)
                for statement in tree.children[block.body]
                    match? tree.nodes[statement]
                        | .node-assign(attribute)
                            if facts.style-declaration-of(unit.reading, statement)
                                continue
                            . setter = own-call(attribute.lhs)
                            if setter != no-fact && facts.calls[setter].form == .call-setter
                                . tracked = tables.live-statement-of(unit.reading, statement)
                                . watching = if tracked then open-trackers(statement) else no-local
                                if tracked
                                    live-actions += LiveTrackers(watching, watching)
                                . given = convert
                                    - attribute.rhs
                                    - .reason-argument
                                    - emit-expression(attribute.rhs)
                                if tracked
                                    live-actions.pop()
                                    attribute-trackers += LiveMember(statement, watching)
                                setter-given += Typed(apart(given, attribute.rhs, true), given.type)
                                continue
                            . name = tree.identifier-name(attribute.lhs)
                            . place = if name then instances.fill-argument(callee, name) else U32.max
                            . fills = filled-parameter(fact, count + written) != U32.max
                            if !fills && place != declared + given
                                refuse(.refused-expression, statement)
                            else
                                . live = tables.live-statement-of(unit.reading, statement)
                                . trackers = if live then open-trackers(statement) else no-local
                                if live
                                    live-actions += LiveTrackers(trackers, trackers)
                                . value = convert
                                    - statement
                                    - .reason-assignment
                                    - emit-expression(attribute.rhs)
                                if fills
                                    value = convert(statement, .reason-argument, value)
                                if live
                                    live-actions.pop()
                                    attribute-trackers += LiveMember(statement, trackers)
                                if !fills
                                    element-filled += element-given.length as U32
                                    given += 1
                                element-given += Typed(apart(value, attribute.rhs, true), value.type)
                                written += 1

────────────────────
+ do give-slots
    - element SyntaxId
    - callee InstanceId

` Gives the constructor of a markup element the function that builds each slot the lines of
` its body give content, in the order the constructor takes them (`builder-value`). Making these
` runs nothing.
. slots = instances.rows[callee].slots.count
. first = instances.signatures[callee].args.count - slots
for offset in 0 .. < slots
    . name = instances.slot-name(callee, offset)
    . line = slot-line(element, name)
    if line == 0
        refuse(.refused-expression, element)
        break
    . built = if tree.holds-fills(line) then emit-choice(line, name) else builder-value(line)
    if built.type != instances.argument-type(callee, first + offset)
        refuse(.refused-conversion, line)
    pending += built.operand

────────────────────
_ do slot-line SyntaxId
    - element SyntaxId
    - name Atom

` The line of a markup element's body that gives the slot of a name content
` (`body-slot-line`), or the name of the element for the name of the function that gives the
` name its object; or none.
match? tree.nodes[element]
    | .node-markup(row)
        if name.text == binder-slot
            = row.id
        = body-slot-line(row.body, name)
= 0

────────────────────
+ do body-slot-line SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId
    - name Atom

` The line of a body that binds the slot of a name, or that gives the default slot, for the
` empty name, element or value, or the body where all of it does, that the type pass made a
` function of, or that forwards the slot of the name; or none.
. default = name.text.length == 0
if body == 0
    = 0
if default && is-closure(facts.node-type(unit.instance, body))
    = body
match? tree.nodes[body]
    | .node-block(block)
        for statement in tree.children[block.body]
            if !default && tree.fills-name(statement, name)
                = statement
            match tree.nodes[statement]
                | .node-markup(line)
                    if is-closure(facts.node-type(unit.instance, statement))
                        if default && line.slot-binding == 0
                            = statement
                        if !default && line.slot-binding != 0 && same-name
                            = statement
                        .. same-name = tree.identifier-name(line.slot-binding) == name
                | .node-markup-slot-forward(line)
                    if !default && tree.identifier-name(line.slot-binding) == name
                        = statement
                ??
                    . attribute = tree.nodes[statement] is .node-assign
                    if default && !attribute && !tree.holds-fills(statement) && is-closure(facts.node-type(unit.instance, statement))
                        = statement
= 0

────────────────────
+ do emit-outlet Operand
    - id SyntaxId
    - name SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId

` A slot outlet, as the function that fills an object with its class's markup mounts it
` (`SlotOutlet`): the node the function that builds the slot gives, the argument this function was
` given for it, or the local a function written in it reads it from, called, given the item the
` outlet names where the slot repeats; or else the one the element its body writes makes, or the
` node its lines are built into (`emit-wrapper`), cast to the type of the slot, which the local the
` outlet's name declares is given. Then each line of its body that assigns is evaluated, in the
` order written, converted as a value assigned to the property it names, and stored there, and the
` one whose value read something tracked is given its live action, owned by the node. The rules the
` outlet applies and the lines that declare styles declare them for the node first, at the outlet's
` own site (`declare-styles`), which is made ready last (`finish-styles`). An outlet that mounts
` nothing gives nothing. One built by the function of the arm it is (`builds-outlet`) gives its name
` nothing, unless that function builds it alone (`builds-outlet-alone`).
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. fact = facts.slot-outlet-of(unit.reading, id)
if fact && fact.chosen != no-instance
    = emit-chosen-outlet(id, fact)
if tree.builds-outlet-alone(id) && !builds-outlet(id)
    emit-outlet-arm(id)
    = nothing
if !fact
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = nothing
if fact.argument == U32.max && fact.held == no-slot && fact.fallback == 0
    = nothing
. type = fact.content
. built = Typed(nothing, no-type)
if fact.picks != no-type
    built = emit-picked-outlet(id, fact, type)
else if fact.argument != U32.max || fact.held != no-slot
    . source = nothing
    . builder = no-type
    if fact.argument != U32.max
        . position = fact.argument
        source = make-operand(.operand-argument, if unit.takes-self then position + 1 else position)
        builder = instances.argument-type(unit.instance, position)
    else
        builder = find-captured(fact.held, id).type
        source = read-captured(fact.held, id, builder).operand
    . item Operand? = null
    if fact.item != 0
        item = convert(fact.item, .reason-argument, emit-expression(fact.item)).operand
    built = call-outlet-builder(id, source, builder, item)
else
    built = emit-outlet-fallback(fact.fallback)
if built.type != type
    refuse(.refused-conversion, id)
    = nothing
. made = built.operand
if names-placed(name) && (!builds-outlet(id) || tree.builds-outlet-alone(id))
    name-element(id, name, built)
. association = declare-styles(id, made, type)
. lively = attribute-trackers.length
match? tree.nodes[body]
    | .node-block(block)
        for statement in tree.children[block.body]
            match? tree.nodes[statement]
                | .node-assign(attribute)
                    if facts.style-declaration-of(unit.reading, statement)
                        continue
                    . name = tree.identifier-name(attribute.lhs)
                    . place = types.property-named(type, name) if name
                    if !place
                        refuse(.refused-statement, statement)
                        break
                    . live = tables.live-statement-of(unit.reading, statement)
                    . trackers = if live then open-trackers(statement) else no-local
                    if live
                        live-actions += LiveTrackers(trackers, trackers)
                    . value = convert(statement, .reason-assignment, emit-expression(attribute.rhs))
                    if live
                        live-actions.pop()
                        attribute-trackers += LiveMember(statement, trackers)
                    store-argument(made, type, place as U32, value.operand, value.type, statement)
for position in lively .. < attribute-trackers.length
    give-again(attribute-trackers[position].member, attribute-trackers[position].trackers, made, type)
while attribute-trackers.length > lively
    attribute-trackers.pop()
finish-styles(id, made, type, association)
= made

────────────────────
_ do call-outlet-builder Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - source Operand
    - builder TypeId
    - item Operand? = null

. holding = hold-outlet-cells(id)
. built = call-builder(id, source, builder, item)
if holding != no-local
    . mark = pending.length
    pending += load-local(holding, id)
    do call-instance(facts.style-runtime.outlet-release, id, mark)
= built

────────────────────
_ do emit-outlet-fallback Typed
    - fallback SyntaxId

=? convert(fallback, .reason-assignment, emit-wrapper(fallback)) if tree.nodes[fallback] is .node-block
= convert(fallback, .reason-assignment, emit-expression(fallback))

────────────────────
_ do emit-picked-outlet Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - fact SlotOutlet
    - type TypeId

. nothing = Typed(make-operand(.operand-void, 0), no-type)
. choice-type = find-captured(fact.held, id).type
. choice = read-captured(fact.held, id, choice-type)
. read = load-property(id, choice.operand, choice-type, program.store-atom("chosen"), true)
if !types.is-optional(read.type) || types.optional-inner(read.type) != fact.picks
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = nothing
if fact.fallback == 0
    = call-outlet-builder(id, payload(id, read).operand, fact.picks)
. result = ir.add-local(layout-of(type, id), false)
. filled = ir.reserve-block()
. empty = ir.reserve-block()
. onward = ir.reserve-block()
branch(present(id, read).operand, filled, empty)
ir.start-block(filled)
. given = call-outlet-builder(id, payload(id, read).operand, fact.picks)
if given.type != type
    refuse(.refused-conversion, id)
    = nothing
store-local(result, given.operand, id)
jump(onward)
ir.start-block(empty)
. fell = emit-outlet-fallback(fact.fallback)
if fell.type != type
    refuse(.refused-conversion, id)
    = nothing
store-local(result, fell.operand, id)
jump(onward)
ir.start-block(onward)
= Typed(load-local(result, id), type)

────────────────────
_ do emit-chosen-outlet Operand
    - id SyntaxId
    - fact SlotOutlet

. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. top = content-hosts.length
if top == 0
    refuse(.refused-statement, id)
    = nothing
. choice = nothing
if fact.argument != U32.max
    . position = fact.argument
    choice = make-operand(.operand-argument, if unit.takes-self then position + 1 else position)
else
    choice = read-captured(fact.held, id, find-captured(fact.held, id).type).operand
. alone = tree.builds-outlet-alone(id)
. arm = if alone then convert(id, .reason-markup-arm, emit-closure(id, fact.arm)).operand else nothing
. mark = pending.length
pending += content-hosts[top - 1].operand
pending += choice
if alone
    pending += arm
    pending += integer(.machine-u8, if fact.fallback != 0 then 1 else 0)
= raising-call(id, fact.chosen, mark).operand

────────────────────
_ do emit-outlet-arm
    - id SyntaxId

. top = content-hosts.length
. slot = channel-slot(id)
if top == 0 || slot == no-slot
    refuse(.refused-statement, id)
    =
. batch = slot - 1
. kept = find-captured(batch, id)
if kept.type != types.void-type
    . root = if content-roots.length != 0 then content-roots[content-roots.length - 1] else make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
    if operand-kind(root) == .operand-void
        refuse(.refused-statement, id)
        =
    keep-captured(batch, root, kept.type, id)
. closure = convert(id, .reason-markup-arm, emit-closure(id))
do call-builder(id, closure.operand, closure.type, content-hosts[top - 1].operand)

────────────────────
_ do call-builder Typed
    - site SyntaxId
    - source Operand
    - builder TypeId
    - item Operand? = null

` A call of what a value of a function type that takes nothing, or the one `item`, holds, given the
` data it holds: the function that builds a slot, as a slot outlet calls it. What runs is not known
` here, so the call is checked for a panic, which the type pass has said of the caller. A type that
` carries errors answers with its value or one of them, and an error leaves the function at the
` call, as the type pass kept.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. fn = function-row(types, builder)
. returns = no-type
if fn != no-type
    match? types.rows[fn]
        | .type-function(row)
            returns = value-returned(row.return-type)
. carried = if fn != no-type && carries(fn) then facts.carried-result(fn) else no-type
. fact = own-call(site)
if returns == no-type || uncarried || fact == no-fact || in-zone || uncaught-panic
    refuse(.refused-expression, site)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
.. uncarried = fn != no-type && carries(fn) && carried == no-type
.. uncaught-panic = !function.may-panic && !in-landing
. layout = layout-of(builder, site)
if layout != tables.layouts.function-layout
    refuse(.refused-expression, site)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. code = load(source, 0, pointer-layout, site)
. data = load(source, tables.layouts.field(layout, 1).offset, managed-layout, site)
. mark = pending.length
pending += data
if item
    pending += item
. answers = layout-of(if carried == no-type then returns else carried, site)
. result = Typed(call(code, site, mark, .callee-value, answers, !in-landing), returns)
if carried != no-type
    result = Typed(result.operand, carried)
    if facts.calls[fact].propagates
        result = propagate-held(site, carried, result.operand)
= result

────────────────────
_ do writes-attributes Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether the body of a markup element gives its constructor an attribute: a line that assigns
` and declares no style.
match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-markup(element)
        match? tree.nodes[element.body]
            | .node-block(block)
                for statement in tree.children[block.body]
                    if tree.nodes[statement] is .node-assign && unstyled
                        = true
                    .. unstyled = !facts.style-declaration-of(unit.reading, statement)
= false

────────────────────
+ do get fills-content Bool

` Whether the function being emitted fills an object with the markup written in its class.
if function.kind != .instance-body || unit.instance == no-instance
    = false
. row = instances.rows[unit.instance]
match? program.modules[row.module].decls[row.decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        = fn.is-content
= false

────────────────────
_ do builds-outlet Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether the function being emitted builds a slot outlet that is a markup branch region.
if function.kind != .instance-body || unit.instance == no-instance
    = false
. row = instances.rows[unit.instance]
match? program.modules[row.module].decls[row.decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        = fn.kind == .branch-arm-decl && fn.syntax == id
= false

────────────────────
+ do emit-region
    - id SyntaxId

` A `do without gc` block outlined, as the reference calls it: its body's function is called with
` the capture `make-capture` makes, crossing into the zone the collector never sees and back.
. callee = region-callee(id)
if callee == no-instance || tables.instance-functions[callee] == no-function
    refuse(.refused-statement, id)
    =
. capture = make-capture(id, callee)
. mark = pending.length
pending += capture
do call-instance(callee, id, mark)

────────────────────
_ do region-callee InstanceId
    - id SyntaxId

` The body of the `do without gc` block at a node, as the type pass recorded it.
. fact = facts.first-call(unit.reading, id)
while fact != no-fact
    if facts.calls[fact].form == .call-function && tables.is-region(facts.calls[fact].callee)
        = facts.calls[fact].callee
    fact = facts.calls[fact].next
= no-instance

────────────────────
+ do emit-region-body

` The body of a `do without gc` block: a function called with the capture made where the block is,
` which returns nothing.
. row = instances.rows[unit.instance]
. body SyntaxId = 0
. declared SyntaxId = 0
match? program.modules[row.module].decls[row.decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        declared = fn.syntax
        body = fn.body
if body == 0 || tables.captures[unit.instance] == unbuilt-environment
    refuse(.refused-function, declared)
    =
unit = unit.received = true
unit = unit.takes-self = true
ir.add-argument(managed-layout)
ir.returns = void-layout
open-environment(declared)
share-self(declared)
emit-block(body)
return-nothing()

────────────────────
_ do keep-element
    - element SyntaxId
    - made Operand
    - type TypeId

` Keeps the object of a markup element in the local no name reaches declared at the element,
` where the functions that read its members by name alone capture it: those written in its
` body, and those that test again the conditions of the style rules written on it.
. slot = channel-slot(element)
if slot != no-slot && is-captured(slot)
    keep-captured(slot, made, type, element)

────────────────────
_ do keep-taken
    - id SyntaxId
    - taken Operand
    - type TypeId

` Keeps what a markup element took of a line of its body that a live action gives again, in
` the local no name reaches after the one that keeps the element, which the action replaces;
` where the element absorbs the line again, that local holds nothing.
. slot = line-keeper(id)
if slot == no-slot
    refuse(.refused-statement, id)
    =
. kept = (slot + 1) as SlotId
. found = find-captured(kept, id)
if found.type == types.void-type
    =
keep-captured(kept, taken, type, id)

────────────────────
+ do emit-ancestor-query

` The function made for an ancestor query of the markup an object is in, which the markup
` runtime runs with the object as its data: the object of the first markup host above the
` object's, from its parent up, that is of the class the query looks for, or nothing, compared
` with what the property holds as one object and stored where they differ, which runs what
` reads the property. It answers whether they differed.
ir.add-argument(managed-layout)
. query = enter-query()
. site = query.site
. object = if tables.is-class(query.level) then tables.layouts.objects[query.level] else no-layout
. property = types.properties[query.place]
if object == no-layout || query.parent == no-instance
    refuse(.refused-function, site)
    =
. field = tables.layouts.field(object, object-header-fields + property.slot)
. held = layout-of(property.type, site)
. cursor-type = instances.signatures[query.parent].returns
. cursor-layout = layout-of(cursor-type, site)
. owner = convert-one(site, facts.conversions[query.hosted], Typed(unit.self, query.level))
. result = ir.add-local(held)
store-local(result, empty-optional(property.type, held).operand, site)
. cursor = ir.add-local(cursor-layout)
. first = pending.length
pending += owner.operand
store-local(cursor, call-instance(query.parent, site, first).operand, site)
. test = ir.reserve-block()
. body = ir.reserve-block()
. next = ir.reserve-block()
. ended = ir.reserve-block()
jump(test)
ir.start-block(test)
. holds = present(site, Typed(load-local(cursor, site), cursor-type))
branch(holds.operand, body, ended)
ir.start-block(body)
. host = payload(site, Typed(load-local(cursor, site), cursor-type))
. target = host-object(site, host.operand, query.target, next)
store-local(result, wrap(site, target, property.type).operand, site)
jump(ended)
ir.start-block(next)
. above = payload(site, Typed(load-local(cursor, site), cursor-type))
. again = pending.length
pending += above.operand
store-local(cursor, call-instance(query.parent, site, again).operand, site)
jump(test)
ir.start-block(ended)
. changed = bits-differ(field-value(unit.self, field, site), load-local(result, site), held, site)
. storing = ir.reserve-block()
. done = ir.reserve-block()
branch(changed, storing, done)
ir.start-block(storing)
put-property(unit.self, field, property, load-local(result, site), site)
jump(done)
ir.start-block(done)
return-value(changed, site)

────────────────────
+ do run-markup-rules
    - type TypeId
    - site SyntaxId

` Runs the rules a class runs once its markup has, on the object the function that fills it
` has filled, as `run-class-rules` runs those of a constructor. A section here is run from the
` table of every class that runs it or of none.
for index in tables.markup-rules-of(type)
    . rule = tables.class-rules[index]
    run-class-rule(rule, facts.lowers-only(rule.level, rule.module, section-of(rule)), site)

────────────────────
+ do run-markup-trigger
    - rule ClassRule
    - trigger MarkupTrigger
    - kept LocalId
    - site SyntaxId

` Runs a `whenever` rule on the markup an object is in once the constructor's body has, as the
` reference compiles it: what the rule keeps for the object holds the object as its markup
` host, the changes it names, made here, and for an ancestor nothing found yet, and then a
` live action of the object's with no trackers, whose callback runs the rule again. The rule
` is registered with the markup runtime, given the object as its host and callbacks that note
` what it looks for, given what it keeps: for children or descendants one as an object is
` added and one as it is removed, with the number of the class looked for, and for an
` ancestor one that looks for it again. The object is converted where the type pass converted
` it for the live actions it owns.
. owned = facts.self-action-of(unit.reading)
if !owned
    refuse(.refused-function, site)
    =
. owner = convert-self(owned.site, .reason-markup-host)
. hosted = tables.layouts.field(rule.kept, 3)
if tables.layouts.is-struct(hosted.layout)
    store-struct(load-local(kept, site), hosted, owner.operand, site)
else
    store(load-local(kept, site), hosted.offset, owner.operand, is-managed-pointer(hosted.layout), site)
. next U32 = 4
if trigger.changes != no-type
    . made = call-instance(trigger.made, site, pending.length)
    store(load-local(kept, site), tables.layouts.field(rule.kept, next).offset, made.operand, true, site)
    next += 1
if trigger.target-id == 0
    . field = tables.layouts.field(rule.kept, next)
    keep-rule-value
        - load-local(kept, site)
        - field
        - empty-optional(trigger.found, field.layout).operand
        - site
. trackers = open-trackers(site)
. action = own-action(load-local(trackers, site), rule.updater, load-local(kept, site), site)
store(load-local(kept, site), tables.layouts.field(rule.kept, 2).offset, action, true, site)
. mark = pending.length
pending += owner.operand
if trigger.target-id != 0
    pending += integer(.machine-u64, tables.target-number(trigger.target-id))
pending += make-callback(rule.add, load-local(kept, site), site)
if trigger.target-id != 0
    pending += make-callback(rule.remove, load-local(kept, site), site)
do call-instance(trigger.register, site, mark)

────────────────────
+ do emit-trigger-change
    - removes Bool

` The function the markup runtime calls with a markup host as one is added below the object a
` `whenever children` or `whenever descendants` rule runs on, or removed, given what the rule
` keeps for the object, as the reference compiles it: where the host's object is of the class
` the rule looks for, and for children where the host's parent is the object's own, the
` object is added to the changes the rule names, or to those removed, and the rule notes that
` the markup changed and runs its live action. It answers true.
. rule = tables.class-rules[function.place]
. trigger = facts.markup-trigger-of(rule.unit)
. site = rule.syntax
unit = unit.source-module = rule.module
if !trigger || rule.kept == no-layout
    refuse(.refused-function, site)
    =
. host-layout = layout-of(trigger.host, site)
ir.add-argument(managed-layout)
ir.add-argument(host-layout)
returns-type = types.bool-type
ir.returns = layout-of(types.bool-type, site)
. kept = make-operand(.operand-argument, 0)
. candidate = ir.add-local(host-layout)
store-local(candidate, make-operand(.operand-argument, 1), site)
. done = ir.reserve-block()
. target = host-object(site, load-local(candidate, site), trigger.target, done)
. children = false
match? tree.nodes[rule.syntax]
    | .node-whenever-rule-syntax(whenever)
        children = whenever.kind.text == "children"
if children
    . mark = pending.length
    pending += load-local(candidate, site)
    . found = call-instance(trigger.parent, site, mark)
    . parent-type = instances.signatures[trigger.parent].returns
    . parent = ir.add-local(layout-of(parent-type, site))
    store-local(parent, found.operand, site)
    . holds = present(site, Typed(load-local(parent, site), parent-type))
    . above = ir.reserve-block()
    branch(holds.operand, above, done)
    ir.start-block(above)
    . host = payload(site, Typed(load-local(parent, site), parent-type))
    . owned = compare
        - site
        - .compare-equal
        - load(host.operand, 0, managed-layout, site)
        - load(kept, tables.layouts.field(rule.kept, 0).offset, managed-layout, site)
    . matched = ir.reserve-block()
    branch(owned, matched, done)
    ir.start-block(matched)
note-change(rule, trigger, kept, target.operand, removes, site)
mark-trigger(rule, trigger, kept, site)
jump(done)
ir.start-block(done)
return-value(integer(.machine-u8, 1), site)

────────────────────
+ do emit-trigger-ancestor

` The function the markup runtime calls where the ancestors of the object a `whenever
` ancestor` rule runs on might have changed, given what the rule keeps for the object, as the
` reference compiles it: the object of the first markup host above the object's, from its
` parent up, that is of the class the rule looks for, or nothing, compared with the one found
` last as one object. Where they differ, the one found last is taken from the changes the rule
` names and the new one added, it is kept, and the rule notes that the markup changed and runs
` its live action. It answers whether they differed.
. rule = tables.class-rules[function.place]
. trigger = facts.markup-trigger-of(rule.unit)
. site = rule.syntax
unit = unit.source-module = rule.module
if !trigger || rule.kept == no-layout
    refuse(.refused-function, site)
    =
. found = trigger
ir.add-argument(managed-layout)
returns-type = types.bool-type
ir.returns = layout-of(types.bool-type, site)
. kept = make-operand(.operand-argument, 0)
. hosted = tables.layouts.field(rule.kept, 3)
. last = tables.layouts.field(rule.kept, if found.changes != no-type then 5 else 4)
. optional = found.found
. cursor-type = instances.signatures[found.parent].returns
. cursor-layout = layout-of(cursor-type, site)
. prior = if tables.layouts.is-struct(last.layout) then snapshot(field-value(kept, last, site), last.layout, site) else load(kept, last.offset, last.layout, site)
. result = ir.add-local(last.layout)
store-local(result, empty-optional(optional, last.layout).operand, site)
. cursor = ir.add-local(cursor-layout)
. first = pending.length
pending += field-value(kept, hosted, site)
store-local(cursor, call-instance(found.parent, site, first).operand, site)
. test = ir.reserve-block()
. body = ir.reserve-block()
. next = ir.reserve-block()
. ended = ir.reserve-block()
jump(test)
ir.start-block(test)
. holds = present(site, Typed(load-local(cursor, site), cursor-type))
branch(holds.operand, body, ended)
ir.start-block(body)
. host = payload(site, Typed(load-local(cursor, site), cursor-type))
. target = host-object(site, host.operand, found.target, next)
store-local(result, wrap(site, target, optional).operand, site)
jump(ended)
ir.start-block(next)
. above = payload(site, Typed(load-local(cursor, site), cursor-type))
. again = pending.length
pending += above.operand
store-local(cursor, call-instance(found.parent, site, again).operand, site)
jump(test)
ir.start-block(ended)
. changed = bits-differ(prior, load-local(result, site), last.layout, site)
. fires = ir.reserve-block()
. done = ir.reserve-block()
branch(changed, fires, done)
ir.start-block(fires)
if found.changes != no-type
    note-ancestor(rule, found, kept, prior, true, site)
    note-ancestor(rule, found, kept, load-local(result, site), false, site)
keep-rule-value(kept, last, load-local(result, site), site)
mark-trigger(rule, found, kept, site)
jump(done)
ir.start-block(done)
return-value(changed, site)

────────────────────
_ do note-ancestor
    - rule ClassRule
    - trigger MarkupTrigger
    - kept Operand
    - value Operand
    - removes Bool
    - site SyntaxId

` Where an ancestor a `whenever ancestor` rule found holds an object, adds it to the changes
` the rule names, or to those removed.
. optional = trigger.found
. holds = present(site, Typed(value, optional))
. noting = ir.reserve-block()
. skipped = ir.reserve-block()
branch(holds.operand, noting, skipped)
ir.start-block(noting)
. held = payload(site, Typed(value, optional))
note-change(rule, trigger, kept, held.operand, removes, site)
jump(skipped)
ir.start-block(skipped)

────────────────────
_ do note-change
    - rule ClassRule
    - trigger MarkupTrigger
    - kept Operand
    - target Operand
    - removes Bool
    - site SyntaxId

` Adds an object to the changes a `whenever` rule on the markup an object is in names, as one
` added or, with `removes`, one removed: to the list the property of that name holds.
if trigger.changes == no-type
    =
. object = if tables.is-class(trigger.changes) then object-layout else no-layout
    .. object-layout = tables.layouts.objects[trigger.changes]
. place = types.property-named
    - trigger.changes
    - program.store-atom(if removes then "removed" else "added")
if object == no-layout || !place
    refuse(.refused-function, site)
    =
. changes = load(kept, tables.layouts.field(rule.kept, 4).offset, managed-layout, site)
. field = tables.layouts.field(object, object-header-fields + types.properties[place].slot)
. mark = pending.length
pending += load(changes, field.offset, field.layout, site)
pending += target
do call-method(trigger.record, site, mark)

────────────────────
_ do mark-trigger
    - rule ClassRule
    - trigger MarkupTrigger
    - kept Operand
    - site SyntaxId

` Notes that the markup a `whenever` rule on the markup an object is in looks at changed, and
` runs the rule's live action, which runs it where it is due.
store(kept, tables.layouts.field(rule.kept, 1).offset, integer(.machine-u8, 1), false, site)
. mark = pending.length
pending += load(kept, tables.layouts.field(rule.kept, 2).offset, managed-layout, site)
do call-method(trigger.schedule, site, mark)

────────────────────
+ do emit-slot-forward

` The function a line that forwards a slot gives in place of the builder it forwards where it
` holds state cells (`SlotForward`), as the reference's `markup-slot-forward` function runs: given
` what it keeps, the builder and the cells, and the item where the slot repeats, it holds the cells
` (`OutletCell`) while the builder runs, and answers what the builder answers.
. row = facts.slot-forwards[function.place]
. layout = tables.slot-forward-layouts[function.place]
. runtime = facts.style-runtime
unit = unit.source-module = instances.rows[row.instance].module
. site = row.line
. fn = function-row(types, row.builder)
. returns = no-type
if fn != no-type
    match? types.rows[fn]
        | .type-function(shape)
            returns = value-returned(shape.return-type)
. carried = if fn != no-type && carries(fn) then facts.carried-result(fn) else no-type
if returns == no-type || (fn != no-type && carries(fn) && carried == no-type)
    refuse(.refused-function, site)
    =
. answers = if carried == no-type then returns else carried
ir.add-argument(managed-layout)
if row.item != no-type
    ir.add-argument(layout-of(row.item, site))
returns-type = answers
ir.returns = layout-of(answers, site)
. kept = make-operand(.operand-argument, 0)
. mark = ir.add-local(layout-of(instances.signatures[runtime.outlet-mark].returns, site))
store-local(mark, call-instance(runtime.outlet-mark, site, pending.length).operand, site)
. index U32
for held in facts.outlet-cells
    if held.instance != row.instance || held.outlet != row.line
        continue
    . first = pending.length
    pending += integer(.machine-u32, tables.state-key-number(facts.scope-cells[held.cell].key))
    pending += load(kept, tables.layouts.field(layout, 2 + index).offset, managed-layout, site)
    do call-instance(runtime.outlet-push, site, first)
    index += 1
. code = load(kept, tables.layouts.field(layout, 0).offset, pointer-layout, site)
. data = load(kept, tables.layouts.field(layout, 1).offset, managed-layout, site)
. first = pending.length
pending += data
if row.item != no-type
    pending += make-operand(.operand-argument, 1)
. result = call(code, site, first, .callee-value, layout-of(answers, site), true)
. held = ir.add-local(layout-of(answers, site))
store-local(held, result, site)
. last = pending.length
pending += load-local(mark, site)
do call-instance(runtime.outlet-release, site, last)
if carried != no-type
    return-held(load-local(held, site))
else
    return-value(load-local(held, site), site)

────────────────────
+ do guard-element Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - element Typed
    - name Atom

. held = element.type
if !function.may-panic && !in-landing
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = element
. made = ir.reserve-block()
. missing = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(id, .compare-not-equal, element.operand, integer(.machine-pointer, 0)), made, missing)
ir.start-block(missing)
raise-text(id, "Named markup element \"${name.text}\" is read before its markup constructs it")
ir.start-block(made)
= Typed(element.operand, held)

────────────────────
+ do emit-markup-read Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - object SyntaxId

` A read of a markup link: the subject, given to the markup runtime's function as a
` `MarkupElement`, and the host it answers, taken where it is one as the class the read gives,
` unchecked, as the reference takes it.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. read = facts.markup-read-of(unit.reading, id)
if !read || (object == 0 && !unit.has-self)
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. subject = Typed(unit.self, if unit.reading != unit.instance then instances.rows[unit.reading].self-type else unit.owner-type)
if object != 0
    subject = emit-expression(object)
. host = convert(id, .reason-argument, subject)
. mark = pending.length
pending += host.operand
. linked = call-instance(read.reader, id, mark)
if read.target == no-type
    = linked
. type = facts.node-type(unit.reading, id)
. layout = layout-of(type, id)
. host-type = types.optional-inner(instances.signatures[read.reader].returns)
. host-layout = layout-of(host-type, id)
. holding = ir.reserve-block()
. empty = ir.reserve-block()
. joined = ir.reserve-block()
. slot = join-slot(layout)
. sides = joins.length
branch(present(id, Typed(linked.operand, instances.signatures[read.reader].returns)).operand, holding, empty)
ir.start-block(holding)
. given = payload(id, Typed(linked.operand, instances.signatures[read.reader].returns))
. made = take(given.operand, tables.layouts.field(host-layout, 0), id)
arrive(id, wrap(id, Typed(made, read.target), type).operand, joined, slot)
ir.start-block(empty)
arrive(id, empty-optional(type, layout).operand, joined, slot)
= Typed(close-joins(joined, sides, layout, slot), type)

────────────────────
+ do filled-parameter U32
    - fact CallFact
    - given U32

` The parameter an argument a call gives fills, or none.
for position in 0 .. < fact.fills.count
    if (facts.call-fills[fact.fills.start + position] as U32) == given
        = position
= U32.max
